hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1487","Muhammad bin Al-Ala bin Kurayb told us strange news, Qubaisa told us, Warqa’ bin Omar told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d. On the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: The man of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood still, so we entered upon him and found him sitting in his room. There was a room in front of him. He said: So he prayed sitting, so we stood behind him and prayed. When he finished the prayer, he said: “If I prayed sitting, then pray sitting, and when I prayed Standing and pray standing, and do not stand as Persia does to its tyrants and its kings.”"
